  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41737266",
      "title": "Storing Uploaded Images & Storing Data in the Database",
      "sourceHash": "cd938eed3930d8306e6f360b0ad613a60c19844696496a1c63aec3556e6592fa",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 2.25,
          "en": "Now the image should be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 5.31,
          "en": "on the file system, not in the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.31,
          "end": 8.07,
          "en": "because storing files in databases is a bad idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.07,
          "end": 9.36,
          "en": "It's bad for performance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.36,
          "end": 12.153,
          "en": "because databases simply aren't built for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.17,
          "end": 15.69,
          "en": "Instead, I wanna store the uploaded files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.69,
          "end": 19.62,
          "en": "in that public folder because any images stored there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.62,
          "end": 23.49,
          "en": "in that images folder will be publicly available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.49,
          "end": 26.643,
          "en": "so they can be rendered on the screen without problems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.96,
          "end": 32.22,
          "en": "And therefore we'll now need to perform a couple of steps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.22,
          "end": 35.19,
          "en": "First, I'll start by getting the extension",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.19,
          "end": 36.75,
          "en": "of the uploaded image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.75,
          "end": 40.02,
          "en": "because it could be a JPEG or PNG file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.02,
          "end": 43.71,
          "en": "So I'll dig into the meal image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.71,
          "end": 45.99,
          "en": "Keep in mind that we're storing that image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.99,
          "end": 49.023,
          "en": "which we got from the form under that image key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.47,
          "end": 54.543,
          "en": "So I'm getting access to that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.55,
          "end": 60.24,
          "en": "And then on that I'll call split to split it on the dot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.24,
          "end": 63.753,
          "en": "and pop the last element, which will be the file extension.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.95,
          "end": 69.6,
          "en": "Next, I also want to generate a unique file name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.6,
          "end": 72.18,
          "en": "and not use the file name of the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.18,
          "end": 74.25,
          "en": "So therefore here what I'll do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.25,
          "end": 77.22,
          "en": "is I'll generate a string with those tactics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.22,
          "end": 80.22,
          "en": "using dot string template literal notation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.22,
          "end": 81.76,
          "en": "which we can use in JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.34,
          "end": 88.34,
          "en": "to create a file name that uses .slug here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.01,
          "end": 93.96000000000001,
          "en": "So meal.slug actually, and then a dot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.96000000000001,
          "end": 95.613,
          "en": "and then the extension.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.02000000000001,
          "end": 99.21000000000001,
          "en": "So now with that we got the file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.21000000000001,
          "end": 102.783,
          "en": "Now we need to write that to a file in that public folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.83,
          "end": 106.56,
          "en": "And we can do that with help of an API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.56,
          "end": 108.273,
          "en": "provided by node JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.19200000000001,
          "end": 113.00999999999999,
          "en": "To be precise, the file system API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.00999999999999,
          "end": 117.57300000000001,
          "en": "And for that I'll import fs from node:fs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.97,
          "end": 123.09,
          "en": "This allows us to work with the file system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 123.09,
          "end": 128.09,
          "en": "We can then use this fs module to call createWriteStream,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.28,
          "end": 130.44,
          "en": "which will create a stream that allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.44,
          "end": 132.393,
          "en": "to write data to a certain file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.5,
          "end": 137.28,
          "en": "Now createWriteStream then needs a path to default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 137.28,
          "end": 138.42000000000002,
          "en": "which you wanna write.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.42000000000002,
          "end": 140.57999999999998,
          "en": "And it'll then return a stream object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.57999999999998,
          "end": 143.253,
          "en": "which you can then use to write to that path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.09,
          "end": 148.44,
          "en": "So regarding that path, I'll create a dynamic string here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.44,
          "end": 151.74,
          "en": "and I'll target public/images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.74,
          "end": 155.613,
          "en": "So this images folder here in this public folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 158.727,
          "end": 161.25,
          "en": "/ and then the fileName",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 161.25,
          "end": 164.223,
          "en": "to which you wanna write must be included in that path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 165.06,
          "end": 167.76,
          "en": "So we can inject that fileName here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.76,
          "end": 170.073,
          "en": "this fileName which we constructed earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 171.99,
          "end": 174.69,
          "en": "With that, we then get a stream which we can store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 174.69,
          "end": 176.22,
          "en": "in a constant or variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 176.22,
          "end": 178.44,
          "en": "in which we can use to write to that path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 178.44,
          "end": 181.5,
          "en": "So to that image in that path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 181.5,
          "end": 183.57,
          "en": "Now we can write to that stream",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.57,
          "end": 186.603,
          "en": "by calling the write method on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 187.47,
          "end": 191.25,
          "en": "And this write method then wants a chunk.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 191.25,
          "end": 193.83,
          "en": "Now what's that chunk?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.83,
          "end": 195.33,
          "en": "In case of our image here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.33,
          "end": 197.76,
          "en": "it means that we should convert the image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.76,
          "end": 201.633,
          "en": "to a so-called buffer to a bufferedImage you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.65,
          "end": 204.15,
          "en": "which might sound fancy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.15,
          "end": 207.3,
          "en": "but which thankfully isn't too difficult to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.3,
          "end": 211.53,
          "en": "You can use that image object, which we have here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.53,
          "end": 214.41,
          "en": "which we're getting from our form after all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.41,
          "end": 217.203,
          "en": "So that image that's being stored under that image key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.1,
          "end": 223.02,
          "en": "And that object has an arrayBuffer method you can call,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 223.02,
          "end": 224.73,
          "en": "which will give you such a buffer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.73,
          "end": 226.73,
          "en": "which we need here for the write method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.57999999999998,
          "end": 230.25,
          "en": "The only tricky thing here is that arrayBuffer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.25,
          "end": 232.02,
          "en": "actually will give you a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.02,
          "end": 234.63,
          "en": "that eventually resolves to that buffer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 234.63,
          "end": 236.613,
          "en": "and therefore we must await this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 237.48,
          "end": 240.51,
          "en": "And in order to use await here, we should add async",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.51,
          "end": 242.823,
          "en": "in front of the saveMeal function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 244.53,
          "end": 247.466,
          "en": "And with that, we then got this bufferedImage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 247.466,
          "end": 249.45,
          "en": "Now this is of type arrayBuffer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 249.45,
          "end": 252.69,
          "en": "and write actually wants a regular buffer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 252.69,
          "end": 255.96,
          "en": "So therefore here we have to call Buffer from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 255.96,
          "end": 257.7,
          "en": "and past this arrayBuffer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 257.7,
          "end": 260.403,
          "en": "so this bufferedImage to it, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.47,
          "end": 266.04,
          "en": "By the way, one other little error I just spotted is here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.04,
          "end": 270.57,
          "en": "where I split my image name to get the extension.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 270.57,
          "end": 275.35,
          "en": "Here, we have to access meal.image.name.split",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 276.69,
          "end": 279.96,
          "en": "because meal.image is simply that image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.96,
          "end": 283.40999999999997,
          "en": "which we get from the form so that image object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.40999999999997,
          "end": 286.26,
          "en": "that's automatically generated by the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 286.26,
          "end": 288.3,
          "en": "and that object will indeed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 288.3,
          "end": 291.09000000000003,
          "en": "have a couple of helpful properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 291.09000000000003,
          "end": 292.68,
          "en": "One of them is the name property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.68,
          "end": 294.87,
          "en": "which carries the name of the image file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 294.87,
          "end": 296.103,
          "en": "that was uploaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 297.87,
          "end": 300.66,
          "en": "So that's something we should change here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 300.66,
          "end": 302.61,
          "en": "But with that back to the stream,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 302.61,
          "end": 307.47,
          "en": "now we're writing this buffer to this path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 307.47,
          "end": 309.63,
          "en": "including this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 309.63,
          "end": 313.98,
          "en": "and this write method now also takes a second argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 313.98,
          "end": 316.47,
          "en": "The first argument is the thing you wanna write.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 316.47,
          "end": 319.56,
          "en": "The second argument is a function that will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 319.56,
          "end": 321.093,
          "en": "once it's done writing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 322.11,
          "end": 324.33,
          "en": "And here we get an error argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 324.33,
          "end": 326.88,
          "en": "which is null if everything worked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 326.88,
          "end": 330,
          "en": "but which will hold some error information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 330,
          "end": 331.653,
          "en": "if something went wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 333.45,
          "end": 338.13,
          "en": "So for here, we should check if error is truthy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 338.13,
          "end": 339.93,
          "en": "So if we have an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 339.93,
          "end": 342.81,
          "en": "and in that case I wanna throw a new Error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 342.81,
          "end": 347.523,
          "en": "where I say, Saving image failed, or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 348.39,
          "end": 353.22,
          "en": "And with that we wrote the image to this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 353.22,
          "end": 357.033,
          "en": "Now we just need to store the overall data in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 357.87,
          "end": 361.65,
          "en": "And for that I'll start by overriding the image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 361.65,
          "end": 366.3,
          "en": "that's stored in my meal object with a path to the image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 366.3,
          "end": 367.92,
          "en": "where we stored it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 367.92,
          "end": 371.07,
          "en": "Because I don't wanna store the image file itself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 371.07,
          "end": 374.4,
          "en": "in a database, databases are not built for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 374.4,
          "end": 377.04,
          "en": "instead I just wanna store the path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 377.04,
          "end": 380.16,
          "en": "Hence I'll overwride the image object in my meal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 380.16,
          "end": 382.2,
          "en": "with that path here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 382.2,
          "end": 386.71,
          "en": "though there you should actually remove this public segment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 387.72,
          "end": 390.9,
          "en": "because all requests for images will be sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 390.9,
          "end": 393.9,
          "en": "to the public folder automatically anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 393.9,
          "end": 397.53,
          "en": "Or put in other words, the content of the public folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 397.53,
          "end": 401.82,
          "en": "will be served as if it were served on the root level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 401.82,
          "end": 403.47,
          "en": "of your Server anyways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 403.47,
          "end": 405.84000000000003,
          "en": "and therefore public shouldn't be included here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 405.84000000000003,
          "end": 408.09000000000003,
          "en": "so that it won't be included later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 408.09000000000003,
          "end": 410.913,
          "en": "when requests for that image will be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 413.13,
          "end": 415.53,
          "en": "But with that, we now finished the preparations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 415.53,
          "end": 418.11,
          "en": "for this meal object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 418.11,
          "end": 420.333,
          "en": "and we can now save it in a database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 421.92,
          "end": 424.74,
          "en": "And to save it, I'll use my db object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 424.74,
          "end": 426.843,
          "en": "and then prepare another statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 428.28,
          "end": 431.73,
          "en": "And here I'll prepare a statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 431.73,
          "end": 434.04,
          "en": "and I'll use this template literal notation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 434.04,
          "end": 436.62,
          "en": "to split it across multiple lines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 436.62,
          "end": 439.93,
          "en": "where I wanna insert some data into the meals table",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 441.33,
          "end": 445.44,
          "en": "and I wanna insert data into the following fields,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 445.44,
          "end": 448.71,
          "en": "into the title, into the summary field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 448.71,
          "end": 453.18,
          "en": "into the instructions field, into the creator field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 453.18,
          "end": 455.89,
          "en": "and the creator email field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 457.35,
          "end": 459.9,
          "en": "and into the image and slug fields.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 459.9,
          "end": 462.84000000000003,
          "en": "So basically into all fields that we configured",
